# MCsquare validation

`pytest` covers the GPU Monte Carlo with self-checking unit tests (`tests/test_dose_mc.py`). Agreement with MCsquare lives in `validation/` and is deliberately outside `pytest`.

- Only run it after changing Monte Carlo physics or transport: `dose_mc.py`, `mc_transport.wgsl`, `mc_materials.npz`, `build_mc_tables.py`, the CT calibration, or the beam model. UI, catalog, or other dose-view changes don't need it.
- `python validation/mcsquare_validate.py fast` (about 30 s) after each physics change; `python validation/mcsquare_validate.py full` (about 10 min) before a PR with physics changes.
- `python validation/mcsquare_validate.py patient` (about 1 min) after changing voxel transport, the CT calibration, the beam model, or anything under `scan_kit/qa/` that feeds the Monte Carlo.
- Don't pass `--write-goldens` unless the user asks. It reruns MCsquare (needs `MCSQUARE_DIR`, many minutes) and is only needed when a case in `CASES` changes or MCsquare is updated.
